{% comment %}
  Value pills driven by a product metafield.

  Same look as the hand-typed pills in `CWC_pdp-key-benefits__block`, but the
  lines come off the product instead of the block, so one template can serve a
  catalogue where every product sells on different points. Defaults to
  `custom.benefit_lines` (list of single line text); the namespace and key are
  settings so a second definition can be pointed at without a code change.

  Renders nothing when the product carries no value — the pills row would
  still contribute its top margin to the column.

  Accepts:
  - block {Object} - the benefit_lines block. Reads settings.namespace,
    settings.key, settings.tone, settings.limit.
  - product {Object} - the product to read the metafield from.

  Usage:
  {% render 'CWC_pdp-benefit-lines__block', block: block, product: product %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign mf_namespace = block.settings.namespace | default: 'custom'
  assign mf_key = block.settings.key | default: 'benefit_lines'
  assign benefit_metafield = product.metafields[mf_namespace][mf_key]

  comment
    A list metafield hands back an array; the single-value types hand back one
    string. Wrapping the lone string keeps the loop below identical for both,
    so pointing this at a plain text definition still works.
  endcomment
  assign benefit_lines = benefit_metafield.value
  unless benefit_metafield.type contains 'list.'
    assign benefit_lines = benefit_lines | split: '~~~single~~~'
  endunless

  assign pill_limit = block.settings.limit | default: 6
  assign tone_mode = block.settings.tone | default: 'tint'
-%}

{%- if benefit_lines != blank and benefit_lines.size > 0 -%}
  <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__pills" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {%- for benefit_line in benefit_lines limit: pill_limit -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign pill_text = benefit_line | strip

        comment
          'alternate' exists because the list has no per-line tone to read —
          banding the pills is the only way to get the two-colour rhythm the
          hand-typed block gets from its tone_1 … tone_6 selects.
        endcomment
        case tone_mode
          when 'alternate'
            assign tone_index = forloop.index0 | modulo: 2
            if tone_index == 0
              assign pill_tone = 'tint'
            else
              assign pill_tone = 'accent'
            endif
          when 'accent'
            assign pill_tone = 'accent'
          else
            assign pill_tone = 'tint'
        endcase
      -%}
      {%- if pill_text != blank -%}
        <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__pill cwc_product-hero-buy-box__pill--{{ pill_tone }}">
          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__pill-mark" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- if pill_tone == 'accent' -%}&#9671;{%- else -%}&#10003;{%- endif -%}
          </span>
          {{ pill_text }}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
